# /etc/svctab - services that live on the disk (DESIGN D11; boot reads this file once the root is up).
# PORT     NICE  PROGRAM [ARGUMENTS]
# A service is started by the first call to its port, and again by the next call after it ended.
# PROGRAM is an absolute path (read as root) or a built-in image (@diskd, @fsd; @zfsd starts /sbin/zfsd); at most
# 6 words in 80 bytes.
# A bad line is reported by boot and skipped. Example (the test message server; msgping(1) calls it):
#ping      0     /bin/msgpingd
# the display server (DESIGN D38): started by the first program of the desktop (zdesk), on that program's console
display   -5    /sbin/displayd
# the sound server (DESIGN D40): Paula's channels for play, modplay and other programs; it ends after 30 s with nothing
# to play (the terminal's bell sounds again) and the next call starts it
audio     -10   /sbin/sndd
# the USB server (DESIGN D46): the xHCI on a Pi 4 / CM4 under Emu68 (otg_mode=1), hubs, USB keyboards and mice; on
# every other machine it says "no USB controller" once and stops until the next boot. lsusb(1) calls it.
usb       -5    /sbin/usbd
